# The build context is the repository root, because the image carries the
# package's own config, agent, scripts and VERSION. Nothing below is copied
# into the image, and keeping it out of the context keeps a test fixture or a
# local note from ever being in reach of a COPY.
#
# Deliberately no *.md rule: agents/sre-fix.md is the agent the runner writes
# into every checkout, and an exclusion that reached it would leave an image
# that builds and then fails its first job.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.superpowers
tests
examples
